    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Raymond Potterton Auctioneers are delighted to present this impressive four-bedroom detached residence, ideally positioned within the popular Cloisters development, close to Kells Town Centre.\n\nExtending to approximately 1,750 sq. ft., the property has recently undergone a comprehensive renovation and is presented to the market in excellent, turnkey condition.\n\nThe works have been completed to a high standard throughout and include a new fitted kitchen, upgraded bathrooms, quality flooring, fixtures and fittings, together with tasteful contemporary décor.\n\nOn entering the property, it is immediately evident that considerable care and attention have gone into the renovation of this fine family home.\n\nThe accommodation is bright, spacious and well proportioned, providing an excellent balance of living and bedroom space over two floors.\n\nThe ground-floor accommodation comprises an entrance hallway, generous lounge, separate study, newly fitted kitchen, dining room, utility room and guest WC. Upstairs, there are four spacious bedrooms, including a master bedroom with ensuite, together with a family bathroom.\n\nExternally, the property benefits from beautifully maintained and fully landscaped gardens to both the front and rear.\n\nA cobble-lock driveway provides ample off-street parking and is complemented by an attractive brick boundary wall.\n\nThe private rear garden provides an ideal space for outdoor dining and family use and also includes a garden shed.\n\nACCOMMODATION\n\nEntrance Hall - 4.7 x 2.07\nWith wooden front door with glass inserts, coving and tiled flooring.\n\nLounge - 5.9 x 3.6\nWith wooden flooring, coving and centrepiece, solid fuel stove with feature fireplace and french doors to\ndining room.\n\nDining Room - 4.5 x 2.9\nWith wooden flooring, coving, centrepiece and French doors to rear garden.\n\nkitchen - 5.4 x 4.5\nWith tiled flooring, built in wall and floor units, integrated oven, hob and extractor fan.\n\nUtility Room - 2.6 x 2.04\nWith tiled flooring, worktop and plumbed for washer/dryer.\n\nGuest w.c. - 1.3 x 0.7\nWith tiled flooring, W.H.B and W.C.\n\nReception Room - 3.7 x 2.5\nWith wooden flooring.\n\nBedroom 1 - 5.2 x 3.6\nWith carpet and fitted wardrobe.\n\nEnsuite\nWith tiled flooring, tiled walls, W.H.B and W.C.\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.6 x 3.5\nWith wooden flooring and fitted wardrobe.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.6 x 3.1\nWith wooden flooring and fitted wardrobe.\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.6 x 3.8\nWith wooden flooring.\n\nBathroom - 2.6 x 2.2\nWith tiled flooring, partially tiled walls, W.H.B and W.C.\n\nFEATURES\n\n• Recently renovated throughout\n• Presented in excellent turnkey condition\n• Approximately 1,750 sq. ft.\n• Four-bedroom detached residence\n• New fitted kitchen\n• Upgraded bathrooms\n• Bright and spacious accommodation\n• Quality fixtures and fittings throughout\n• Oil-fired central heating\n• Fully alarmed\n• Landscaped front and rear gardens\n• Cobble-lock driveway\n• Attractive brick boundary wall\n• Overlooking a large green area\n• Elevated front-row position\n• Quiet cul-de-sac setting\n• Mature and well-established development\n• Within easy reach of Kells Town Centre\n• Excellent access to the M3 motorway and Dublin\n\nDIRECTIONS\n\nFrom Kells Town Centre, travel out the Oldcastle Road and continue to the entrance of The Cloisters development. On entering the development, proceed towards the front-row cul-de-sac, where the property can be identified by our “For Sale” sign."
      },
